# REPO SOVEREIGNTY: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> Consolidates `repo_governance.mdc`. One rule, absolute authority.

## 1. THE SYNC GUARANTEE
Before any deep work session begins:
```bash
git fetch origin && git status   # Verify clean state
git remote -v                    # Confirm remote === Infinity Protocol repo
```

## 2. MILESTONE PUSH PROTOCOL
Upon reaching any milestone (Protocol/Logic/UI/Deploy/Pre-Flight), the Agent MUST:
```bash
git add -A
git commit -m "type(scope): description [Milestone: Type]"
git push origin main
```
- No exceptions. Every session ends with a clean remote state.
- Commit message format: `feat|fix|chore|docs|refactor|perf(scope): description`

## 3. BRANCH & CLEANLINESS GOVERNANCE
- **Never commit**: `node_modules/`, `.env*` (except `.env.example`), `dist/`, `.next/`, `*.log`
- **Purge before sync**: `.bak`, `tmp*`, `*.orig` files
- **Gitignore**: Verify `.gitignore` is complete before first commit in any new workspace

## 4. ERROR RECOVERY
| Symptom | Action |
|---|---|
| `index.lock` exists | `rm -f .git/index.lock` |
| Push rejected (non-fast-forward) | `git pull --rebase origin main` then repush |
| `git push --force` | ONLY if 100% certain this is the sovereign state |
| Hung process | Kill, check `git status`, never blindly retry |

## 5. BACKUP MANDATE
- Every project MUST have at least one remote (GitHub `ccceoscott/*`).
- For critical projects: configure secondary backup (Bitbucket, GCS bucket, or automated clone).

## 6. AUTOMATION
- `dv broadcast` — propagate rules to all workspaces
- `dv doctor` — workspace health check
- `dv locksheet` — regenerate SOVEREIGN_LOCK checksums
